## Curated builds

Reviewed against patch 2.1.67 on 2026-05-13. The live patch is 2.2.16a, so these have not been re-read against it yet.

### Ranked CDR Control (Mid)

- Items: Magic Boots, Glowing Wand, Fleeting Time, Wishing Lantern, Divine Glaive, Blood Wings
- Core: Magic Boots, Glowing Wand, Fleeting Time
- Emblem: Mage Emblem with Inspire, Bargain Hunter, Impure Rage
- Battle spell: Flicker
- Flex: Arcane Boots over Magic Boots when Use when your lane is free and early Magic Penetration matters more than faster global cooldown cycles.; Enchanted Talisman over Fleeting Time when Use when your team is not converting early ultimates into assists and you need stable mana plus maximum CDR instead of resets.; Winter Crown over Blood Wings when Use when dive assassins can still reach you after Flicker and your passive shield is being forced before objectives.
- Total cost: 11130 gold

Default ranked setup that buys early anti-heal, then uses Fleeting Time resets to turn Zetian's global stun into repeated objective pressure.

### Front-to-Back Damage (Mid)

- Items: Arcane Boots, Glowing Wand, Lightning Truncheon, Wishing Lantern, Holy Crystal, Divine Glaive
- Core: Glowing Wand, Lightning Truncheon, Wishing Lantern
- Emblem: Mage Emblem with Rupture, Bargain Hunter, Lethal Ignition
- Battle spell: Flicker
- Flex: Magic Boots over Arcane Boots when Use when your team needs more frequent global stuns and you can delay the early Magic Penetration spike.; Blood Wings over Holy Crystal when Use when assassins are trading health to reach you and a regenerating shield is worth more than maximum Magic Power.; Ice Queen Wand over Lightning Truncheon when Use when your front line can protect you and the fight is decided by keeping tanks inside Phoenix Descent.
- Total cost: 12210 gold

Higher-damage path for slower front-to-back games where Zetian can stand deep, stack repeated magic hits, and punish Magic Defense buys.

### CC Safety Utility (Mid)

- Items: Magic Boots, Enchanted Talisman, Glowing Wand, Ice Queen Wand, Divine Glaive, Winter Crown
- Core: Magic Boots, Enchanted Talisman, Glowing Wand, Ice Queen Wand
- Emblem: Mage Emblem with Inspire, Bargain Hunter, Impure Rage
- Battle spell: Purify
- Flex: Fleeting Time over Ice Queen Wand when Use when your team reliably converts every ultimate into assists and reset uptime is stronger than extra slows.; Blood Wings over Winter Crown when Use when the enemy has poke and chip damage but lacks instant dive that forces stasis.; Wishing Lantern over Divine Glaive when Use against high-HP front lines before they commit heavily to Magic Defense.
- Total cost: 10750 gold

Defensive utility path for CC-heavy games where Purify, mana stability, slows, and stasis matter more than burst ceiling.

